# Chroma library, modern Earth: NATIONAL ROUTE ENCOUNTERS, part b (v25 decision #11, cut item 3; draft 10-23).
# Pours into chroma-library/earth_national-*.lib (built as earth_national.py; briefs/NATIONAL.md). Drafts only.
# The last seven routes of world_fit.json national.routes: opportunity_patron, rallying_voice, national_virtuoso,
# commander, living_land_steward, living_heritage_keeper, community_weaver. Four moments each, all with route: <key>:
# the route's dilemma at the local step (rungs 0 1), the wider step (2 3) and the national step (4), and one crisis
# (kind setback, rungs any). Each route mixes practice, a contest or chance, a fork kind and the setback.
# The national step reaches one of the three, never all: influence (patron, voice, commander), recognition (virtuoso,
# heritage keeper), authority (land steward, community weaver).
# Layout: every moment is a life event in the balance layout: W U B R G once each, then one full cross cycle,
#   s1 = W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W (odd moments)      s2 = W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U (even moments)
# The commander route is rescue, readiness, discipline and answering to civilian rule: no fighting and no war.
# The land acts through weather, water, soil, growth and animals; it never judges.

# ================================================================ OPPORTUNITY PATRON (one breakthrough versus a portfolio)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local: practice (s1)

== the monthly round of the small ventures backed
tier: life event
route: opportunity_patron
shape: any
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-80
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: money, community
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, friend, mentor
earth: the monthly round of the small ventures {N} has backed in town, and one of them wants everything left
tribal: the round of the families {N} has lent seed and tools to, and one of them asks for all that is left
magic: the round of the workshops {N} has staked with coin, and one of them asks for the whole purse
scene: Once a month {N} goes round the small ventures backed with spare savings: {neighbour}'s bakery, a bicycle repair shop, a young singer's first recordings. This month the bakery asks for everything left in the pot for a second oven, sure it is the one that will take off. The others would get nothing until spring.
scene tribal: Each moon {N} visits the families lent seed and tools from {Ns} own store. This time one household asks for all that is left, to clear a new field they swear will feed half the camp; the others would go without until the thaw.
scene magic: Each month {N} calls on the workshops staked with a little coin: a glassblower, a scribe, a young lute player. This month the glassblower asks for the whole purse to build a second furnace, certain it will make a name; the others would wait a year.
- W | keep the shares as agreed at the start, the same for each venture | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | go through each venture's books properly before moving any money | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | put the whole pot behind the bakery, the one most likely to pay | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 55
- R | back the singer instead, the long shot nobody else would touch | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | skip the round this month and let each venture find its own feet | v: security, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- W>U | write down a rule for who gets what, and test it on this month | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson a rule beats a hunch | chance: 75
- U>B | give the bakery half, on condition of a written plan for the oven | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
- B>R | have all three make their case over supper, and back the best pitch | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R>G | spend the evening helping at the repair shop instead of counting | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
- G>W | ask the other two whether they would wait, and abide by their answer | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
works: By spring the choice has settled, and {N} has a clearer sense of which kind of backer to be.
works: Nobody gets everything they asked for, and nobody walks away, which in a small town counts.
fails: The big hope stays a plan, and the money sits where it helps nobody.
fails: One of the three takes the decision personally, and the next visit there is stiff.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wider: cost, fork pay (s2)

== the one big backing that would cost the eight small ones
tier: life event
route: opportunity_patron
shape: any
kind: cost
rungs: 2 3
fork: pay
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 24-82
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: money, work
horizon: months
roles: ally, colleague, partner
earth: the fund now backs people across the region, and its one big hope needs most of what it holds
tribal: the shared store now feeds families across the valley, and one great venture would need most of it
magic: the patrons' purse now reaches towns across the province, and one bold workshop would drain it
scene: The small fund {N} set up with {ally} and two others now backs people in towns across the region. A young engineer's water pump, backed early, needs a far larger sum to reach the factories; to pay for it the other funders want to pull out of eight small backings. They decide at the quarterly meeting, two weeks off.
scene tribal: The store {N} keeps with {ally} and two other families now lends to camps across the valley. A young builder's fish weir, backed early, would need most of the store to build at full size, and eight small loans would have to be called back. The families meet at the full moon.
scene magic: The purse {N} keeps with {ally} and two merchant houses now stakes workshops across the province. A young artificer's water engine, staked early, needs a sum that would mean closing eight small stakes. The patrons meet in a fortnight.
- W | pay the share the fund's own rules allow, and not a coin more | v: conformity, security | aim: pay | cost: money .3, time .2, family .1 | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 75
- U | pay, after an outside engineer checks the design really works at scale | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: pay | cost: money .3, time .3, family .1 | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | put in personal savings on top, and take a bigger stake in the big hope | v: power, achievement | aim: pay | cost: money .6, time .3, family .3 | foot: means money-.10 | chance: 55
- R | refuse the big bet, and keep backing the eight odd small ones | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: refuse | foot: lesson many small seeds | chance: 70
- G | step back from the fund, and keep only the backings close to home | v: security, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: lesson a small circle holds | chance: 85
- W>B | pay, and ask the board for a seat to watch where the money goes | v: conformity, power | aim: pay | cost: money .3, time .4, family .2 | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 65
- U>R | bring in a second fund to share the big backing, and keep the small ones alive | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: refuse | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- B>G | pay, but promise each of the eight a way back in within two years | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: pay | cost: money .4, time .3, family .2 | foot: door kept your word | chance: 60
- R>W | hold off a season, and put the question to everyone the fund backs | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
- G>U | hand the fund to the others, and keep what it taught for the next one | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 85
works not G G>U: The meeting ends late with a decision {N} can defend, and the cost is out in the open.
works: Whatever was chosen, the people backed hear it straight, and most of them respect that.
fails not G G>U: The money is tighter than the sums said, and two of the small ones feel dropped.
fails: For weeks afterwards {N} wonders whether the one or the eight was the better bet.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- national: chance, fork take (s1); influence

== the chair of the country's grants panel
tier: life event
route: opportunity_patron
shape: any
kind: chance
rungs: 4
fork: take
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: work, publiclife
horizon: years
roles: rival, colleague, partner
earth: a national foundation asks {N} to chair the panel that decides what it funds across the country
tribal: the moot of the clans asks {N} to say which ventures the shared stores of every clan will feed
magic: the crown's treasury asks {N} to sit at the head of the table that decides which works the realm stakes
scene: A national foundation asks {N} to chair its grants panel, which decides which work across the country gets money. The panel's custom is one large prize a year for a single breakthrough; {N} has always spread money thin and wide. The answer is due at the month's end, and it would mean long reading weeks, travel, and letting the local fund go to others.
scene tribal: The moot of all the clans asks {N} to say which ventures the shared stores of every clan will feed. The custom is to feed one great work each year; {N} has always fed many small ones. They want an answer before the geese go.
scene magic: The crown's treasury asks {N} to head the table that decides which works the realm will stake. Its custom is one grand stake a year; {N} has always staked many small workshops. The answer is wanted by the month's end.
- W | accept, once the panel's rules on conflicts of interest are written down | v: conformity, universalism | aim: take | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 75
- U | ask to sit one round as an ordinary member first, and decide after | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: lesson see the table first | chance: 70
- B | accept, and steer the panel toward one bold prize a year | v: power, achievement | aim: take | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 60
- R | accept on the spot, and turn the first round upside down | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: take | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G | turn it down, and keep backing people close enough to visit | v: benevolence, security | aim: decline | foot: mark stayed home | chance: 85
- W>U | accept, if the panel publishes why each grant was made | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: take | foot: lesson open reasons build trust | chance: 70
- U>B | ask for a year's delay to hand the local fund over properly | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: ease | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 75
- B>R | stand for the chair against the board's own candidate, and win it outright | v: power, stimulation | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- R>G | accept, and split the one big prize into forty small grants | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: take | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 55
- G>W | let the national road go, and train a younger backer for the local fund | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: stop | foot: person colleague | chance: 85
works not G G>W U>B: The first round of grants goes out, and some of it lands where nobody had looked before.
works: Whatever {N} chose, it was chosen with a clear head, and the local fund is in good hands.
fails not G G>W U>B: The board pushes back on every change, and the first year is mostly arguing over rules.
fails: Doubt follows the choice for a while, as it does after any large one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- crisis: setback (s2)

== the backed venture that went under in public
tier: life event
route: opportunity_patron
shape: any
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: money, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, ally, colleague
earth: the venture {N} backed hardest fails in public, and the other backers want {Ns} name off it
tribal: the venture {N} fed most from the store fails before the whole valley, and the families want someone to blame
magic: the workshop {N} staked most fails before the whole town, and the other patrons want {Ns} name off the stake
scene: The venture {N} backed hardest, {friend}'s workshop, has failed in public: the money is gone, the local paper makes a meal of it, and the other backers want {Ns} name off everything. {friend} asks for a little more, to wind down properly and pay the staff what they are owed.
scene tribal: The venture {N} fed most from the shared store, {friend}'s new fishing ground, has failed before the whole valley. The other families want the store's loss named, and {friend} asks for a little more seed to see the helpers through the winter.
scene magic: The workshop {N} staked most, {friend}'s, has failed before the whole town, and the other patrons want {Ns} name struck from the stake. {friend} asks for a last purse, to pay the journeymen what they are owed.
- W | honour every promise made to the workshop's staff, out of the fund's reserve | v: conformity, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 75
- U | go through what went wrong with {friend}, line by line, and write it up | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | buy what can be saved of the workshop cheaply, and start again with it | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 55
- R | back {friend}'s next idea at once, before the talk dies down | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | stop backing ventures, and stay a friend to {friend} through the worst | v: benevolence, security | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
- W>B | stand beside {friend} at the creditors' meeting, and answer every question | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 65
- U>R | tell the story of the failure openly at the next backers' evening | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson failures teach the room | chance: 65
- B>G | cover the staff's last wages personally, then rebuild the fund slowly | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means money-.08 | chance: 60
- R>W | ride out the gossip, and keep every other backing exactly on schedule | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 70
- G>U | let the fund go, and keep the eye for people it trained | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: lesson the eye stays sharp | chance: 85
works: Slowly the talk moves on, and the people {N} backs know now what kind of backer {N} is.
works: A season later the worst is past, and {friend} still answers when {N} calls.
fails: The talk lasts longer than it should, and two promising people take their ideas elsewhere.
fails: It is a slow, sour season, and every new proposal looks like the last one.

# ================================================================ RALLYING VOICE (disruptive pressure versus negotiation)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local: practice (s1)

== the weekly meeting about the cut late bus
tier: life event
route: rallying_voice
shape: any
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-80
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: elder, colleague, rival
earth: the weekly residents' meeting about the late bus the town means to cut, and {N} keeps speaking at it
tribal: the nightly fire where the camp argues over the elders' plan to close the river crossing after dark
magic: the weekly gathering in the guildhall over the lord's plan to close the night gate
scene: Every Tuesday the residents meet in the library annex about the late bus the town plans to cut, the one night-shift workers take home. {N} has spoken at the last three meetings, and people now wait to hear what {N} will say. The council has offered talks in a month; some want to block the depot now.
scene tribal: Every night the camp argues at the fire over the elders' plan to close the river crossing the herders use after dark. People have begun to wait for {N} to speak. The elders will hear one voice at the next moon; some want to sit on the crossing now.
scene magic: Every week the craftsfolk crowd the guildhall over the lord's plan to close the night gate the late workers use, and they have begun to wait for {N} to speak. The steward offers an audience next month; some want to hold the gate open by standing in it.
- W | prepare a short, fair statement of the case, and read it at every meeting | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | gather the night workers' hours and numbers, and bring them to the meeting | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | ask the council for a seat at the talks, as the residents' spokesperson | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | call for everyone to fill the depot yard on Friday night | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 55
- G | sit this week out, and let others take the floor | v: security, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- W>U | take the talks offered, with the night workers' figures in hand | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson numbers open doors | chance: 75
- U>B | find out who on the council could save the bus, and work on that one | v: self-direction, power | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- B>R | announce a march for next week, and use the threat to bring the talks sooner | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- R>G | spend the evening on the last bus, talking with the people who ride it | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- G>W | ask the oldest residents what worked last time, and follow their way | v: tradition, conformity | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 75
works: People leave the meeting with something to do, and more of them come next week.
works: Nothing is saved yet, but those in charge now know the names of the people it would hurt.
fails: The meeting goes round in circles, and two people walk out before the end.
fails: Nothing moves this week, and the closing date stays where it was.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wider: round, fork round (s2)

== the hall that will not take the movement's booking
tier: life event
route: rallying_voice
shape: any
kind: round
rungs: 2 3
fork: round
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-82
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: community, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: colleague, friend, rival
earth: the regional hall cancels the movement's bookings after the last rally, and the talks stall; but there is {aim.round}
tribal: the elders of the next valley refuse the movement a place at their fire; but there is {aim.round}
magic: the provincial court bars the movement from its hall after the last gathering; but there is {aim.round}
scene: The movement has grown past the town: buses come from four others now. After the last rally ran late and loud, the regional hall cancels every booking, and the council says it will only talk with people who come through proper channels. {N} has heard of {aim.round}, and the next rally date is a month off.
scene tribal: The movement now draws people from four valleys. After the last gathering ran loud into the night, the elders of the next valley refuse it a place at their fire and will only hear a proper envoy. {N} has heard of {aim.round}, and the next gathering is a moon off.
scene magic: The movement now draws craftsfolk from four towns. After the last gathering filled the square past curfew, the provincial court bars it from the hall and will only hear petitions sent in proper form. {N} has heard of {aim.round}, and the next gathering is a month away.
- W | register the movement properly, and use {aim.round} meanwhile | v: conformity, security | aim: round | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 70
- U | check who runs {aim.round} and what they would ask of the movement | v: self-direction, security | aim: round | foot: lesson ask what a host wants | chance: 70
- B | go straight to {aim.round}, and let the council see the crowd it turned away | v: power, achievement | aim: round | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 55
- R | hold the rally in the street outside the closed hall, the same night | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: round | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | let the rallies rest for a season, and keep the town groups meeting | v: security, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | take the council's offer of talks, with the crowd's demands in writing | v: conformity, power | aim: round | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- U>R | move the next rally to {aim.round}, and make it a different kind of day | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: round | foot: lesson a new room, new rules | chance: 60
- B>G | apologise for the noise, and ask the hall for a smaller booking later on | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: mark owned up | chance: 70
- R>W | hand the lead to someone steadier, and step back from the movement | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: stop | foot: lesson a voice can pass on | chance: 85
- G>U | let the marching go, and keep the friends it made | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
works not G B>G R>W G>U: The new way in draws a different crowd, and the council's tone changes a little.
works: The block matters less than it did, and the movement keeps its shape.
fails not G B>G R>W G>U: The new way is harder than it sounded, and fewer come from the far towns.
fails: Some in the movement call the choice weak, others call it reckless, and {N} hears both.

