- U>R | raise the money for the damage at a street concert that weekend | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
- B>G | pay for one shop's window personally, and ask the movement to cover the rest | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 60
- R>W | tell the next meeting plainly what the movement will not do | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: lesson a crowd needs limits | chance: 70
- G>U | let the movement go on without {N}, and keep what it taught about crowds | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: lesson crowds need care | chance: 85
works: The street is mended within the month, and the movement comes out of it with stricter stewards.
works: Some trust is lost and some is earned back, and {N} knows now what a crowd can do.
fails: The story follows the movement for months, and every rally is asked about that night.
fails: The split over the apology hardens, and a few old friends stop coming.

