earth: the restored river corridor reaches three farms whose owners say no; but there is {aim.round}
tribal: the restored stream reaches the grazing of three families who will not give way; but there is {aim.round}
magic: the restored river reaches three estates whose lords refuse it; but there is {aim.round}
scene: The restoration has worked: otters are back on the river, and other towns ask {N} to come and advise. But the corridor downstream crosses three farms, and their owners say no: they lost land to the last scheme. The grant for the next stretch runs out at the year's end, and {N} has heard of {aim.round}.
scene tribal: The restored stream runs clear again, the fish are back, and other camps ask {N} to show them how. But below the camp it crosses the grazing of three families, who say no: they lost pasture the last time. The season for the work ends with the first frost, and {N} has heard of {aim.round}.
scene magic: The restored river runs clear, the otters are back, and other towns send for {N}. But downstream it crosses three estates whose lords refuse it, remembering land lost to the last scheme. The guild's purse for the work closes at the year's end, and {N} has heard of {aim.round}.
- W | apply for {aim.round} through the proper process, with the farmers informed | v: conformity, security | aim: round | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 70
- U | look into {aim.round}: what it costs the farms and what it gives the river | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: round | foot: lesson count both sides first | chance: 70
- B | ask the regional board to require the corridor, whatever the farmers say | v: power, achievement | aim: round | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | take {aim.round} at once, and let the farmers see the results for themselves | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: round | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G | let the downstream stretch wait, and look after what is already restored | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | draw up a written agreement with each farm: what is paid, what is kept | v: conformity, power | aim: round | foot: means money-.05 | chance: 60
- U>R | design a narrower corridor that spares the farms' best fields, and try it on one | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: round | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B>G | spend the winter at the farmers' kitchen tables before asking anything | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
- R>W | hand the corridor to the regional trust, and step back from it | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: stop | foot: lesson others can carry it | chance: 85
- G>U | let the wider work go, and keep tending the home stretch for good | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 85
works not G B>G R>W G>U: One farm signs, then a second, and the river starts to come back below them.
works: The choice holds, and the restored stretch keeps doing well whatever the farms decide.
fails not G B>G R>W G>U: The new way is slower than it looked, and the money runs down while the talks go on.
fails: The farmers remember the choice, and it takes a long while for the coldness to lift.

