magic: a storm flood breaks the new banks and buries a farmer's field under silt
scene: A winter flood, the worst in years, broke through the banks {N} restored and spread silt over {neighbour}'s best field. The reserve itself came through well; the farm did not. {neighbour} says the scheme caused it, the papers are asking, and the trust meets on Monday to decide what to do.
scene tribal: The spring melt came fast and broke through the banks {N} built up, and spread mud over {neighbour}'s best grazing. The stream's own ground came through; the grazing did not. {neighbour} says the new banks caused it, and the camp will talk of it at the fire tonight.
scene magic: A storm flood broke through the banks {N} restored and buried {neighbour}'s best field under silt. The reserve came through well; the farm did not. {neighbour} blames the scheme before the whole market, and the guild meets in three days.
- W | own the reserve's part, and follow the trust's rules on putting it right | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 70
- U | get the flood studied properly, to show what the banks did and did not do | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | argue the flood would have come anyway, and keep the scheme as it is | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 50
