- R>W | call a meeting in the village hall, and take every question standing | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 65
- G>U | hand the reserve to the trust, and keep what the flood taught about water | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: stop | foot: lesson floods redraw the map | chance: 85
works: By summer the field is clearing, the banks are rebuilt, and {neighbour} is talking again.
works: The season is hard, and {N} comes out of it knowing the river better.
fails: The argument goes on through the spring, and other farmers start to doubt the scheme.
fails: The silt takes longer to clear than anyone said, and patience wears thin on both sides.

