scene: The last rush-weaver in the district has died, and the family is selling the shed, the tools and the drying racks. People from towns across the region now write to {N} about lost crafts, and this is one. Buying it all and learning from the notebooks would take savings and two years of evenings; a souvenir maker has also made an offer, to make the baskets by machine. The family wants an answer by the month's end.
