- R | throw out the agenda and let each group say what it actually needs | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 60
- G | leave the rota as it is for the winter, and change nothing yet | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | set the rota, with a firm vote for every group however small | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: lesson a vote each | chance: 65
- U>R | try the single rota on one route for a month, and see what breaks | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson pilot before rule | chance: 60
- B>G | let the big group run the vans, and the small ones keep their own kitchens | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- R>W | turn the meeting into a shared meal first, then settle the rota | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- G>U | visit the two small groups at home before anything is decided | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 70
works: The winter rota is set by midnight, and every group leaves feeling it was heard.
works: The web holds for another month, a little tighter where it needed to be.
fails: The meeting runs late and bad-tempered, and one small group threatens to leave.
fails: The rota is set, but nobody is quite happy with it, and it shows by midwinter.

